And I don't know if any of you are fans of the TV show Six Feet Under, but you'll know from this TV show that there are many different kinds of caskets.

65
00:04:05,150 --> 00:04:06,230
So a casket is a box.

66
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:12,450
You can have fancy caskets or you can have wooden caskets that are very simple, like pine.

67
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:18,110
And basically this is the box that the person's body will go into when they're buried.

68
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:19,520
Right.

69
00:04:19,520 --> 00:04:20,520
Very good.

70
00:04:20,520 --> 00:04:21,750
So that is called a casket.

71
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:29,870
Well moving on, a new trend I would say in many countries and many people around the world don't want to be buried.

72
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:31,230
So what happens?

73
00:04:31,430 --> 00:04:33,190
You get cremated.

74
00:04:33,830 --> 00:04:34,350
Cremated.

75
00:04:34,570 --> 00:04:37,250
So this is the option for people who are not buried.

76
00:04:37,830 --> 00:04:41,030
In some countries, China for example, I don't think you can be buried.

77
00:04:41,170 --> 00:04:44,390
You have to be cremated because there's an issue of space.

78
00:04:45,400 --> 00:04:56,000
And this is an option for most people where basically your friend or your loved one, their body is burned and you can collect the remains afterwards.

79
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:56,460
They're very small.

80
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:57,000
They're ashes.

81
00:04:57,840 --> 00:04:59,920
So it's like a burning process.

82
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:00,920
Okay, interesting.

