88
00:05:20,470 --> 00:05:26,970
But an urn is a special kind of pot, okay, or a vessel to hold things in.

89
00:05:27,430 --> 00:05:33,630
So for example, in this case we have a cremation urn that is a special pot, usually very beautiful.

90
00:05:34,450 --> 00:05:41,390
Sometimes there's a name on it with the deceased person's ashes, his or her remains.

91
00:05:41,930 --> 00:05:42,830
Okay, very good.

92
00:05:43,080 --> 00:05:52,400
So as you said, it's kind of like a vase or a pot, something very nice and small where you have the person's ashes.

93
00:05:52,910 --> 00:05:55,470
All right, so now we know what happened during the funeral.

94
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:59,390
We know what happens, how you maybe cremate the person or you put them in a casket.

95
00:06:00,150 --> 00:06:01,810
And well, what happens afterwards?

96
00:06:02,610 --> 00:06:04,610
Well, afterwards you have a memorial service.

97
00:06:05,470 --> 00:06:09,710
Okay, so many people want to know what's the difference between a funeral and a memorial service.

98
00:06:10,870 --> 00:06:21,080
In my mind, a funeral is very quiet and sad and you have some respectful words and you usually put the casket into the ground or have some kind of ceremony.

99
00:06:21,320 --> 00:06:29,420
But a memorial service is an opportunity to talk to friends and family, to eat some food, to have some drinks, to talk about the person who died.

100
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:32,120
It's almost like the party, if that makes sense.

101
00:06:32,740 --> 00:06:33,600
Yeah, exactly.

102
00:06:34,400 --> 00:06:51,080
It's a get together of people who obviously are trying to give support to their friends or their family members who lost that person, but also to talk about that person in a good way and all the great memories they had.

103
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:57,200
I guess that's why it's called a memorial service because you remember and you give out your memories about that person.

104
00:06:57,200 --> 00:06:58,200
Exactly.

105
00:06:58,200 --> 00:06:58,460
Okay, great.

