179
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:47,220
This is a great verb.

180
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:54,260
This is a verbal phrase that we hear a lot with documents and wills and things like this.

181
00:11:54,980 --> 00:12:01,940
Basically, to sort out means to solve problems or to fix or to amend.

182
00:12:02,650 --> 00:12:06,950
For example, have you sorted out that problem you had with your plane tickets?

183
00:12:07,990 --> 00:12:08,170
Okay.

184
00:12:08,570 --> 00:12:09,110
To sort out.

185
00:12:09,350 --> 00:12:13,990
So have you fixed those problems or have you solved those problems that you had with your plane tickets?

186
00:12:14,270 --> 00:12:17,130
To sort out, to fix, to make arrangements for.

187
00:12:17,290 --> 00:12:18,250
Very, very useful phrase.

